    {
      "id": "9ffb0f27c8eeda2e1fe9d65d8d47e12d973ad811",
      "short_id": "9ffb0f27",
      "created_at": "2021-02-16T09:00:12.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "23a5f6a17767c39a7ed04df438ae3b4bf1fe90d8"
      ],
      "title": "GitHub CI, CMake: override the definition of cmake_build.",
      "message": "GitHub CI, CMake: override the definition of cmake_build.\n\nOverriding the definition of the rpmbuild macro cmake_build on the\ncommand line, so that it doesn't include the string \"--verbose\", should\nprevent cmake --build from being run with --verbose, and thus prevent it\nfrom running Ninja with the -v flag, and thus prevent a bunch of extra\nnoisy output from being produced for every build command, and thus\nprevent the build log from hitting GitLab's 4MB limit.\n\nUnlike piping the output of \"ninja rpm-package\" to sed, this means that\nthe exit status of \"ninja rpm-package\", rather than the exit status of\nsed, is tested.\n",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "authored_date": "2021-02-16T00:33:50.000-08:00",
      "committer_name": "Guy Harris",
      "committer_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "committed_date": "2021-02-16T09:00:12.000+00:00",
